  "issue": {
    "body": "Hi folks,\r\n\r\nCurrently, the `TestClient` is built as a subclass of `requests.Session`.\r\n\r\nWhat would be thoughts on migrating to [HTTPX](https://github.com/encode/httpx)?\r\n\r\n- Is this a good idea at all?\r\n- Should the `TestClient` be built *around* HTTPX, or should it eventually be *replaced* by HTTPX and its ASGI support?\r\n\r\nAs of today, there are definitely blockers to a full migration. An important one is that HTTPX doesn't support WebSocket yet (see https://github.com/encode/httpx/issues/304), while `TestClient` does.\r\n\r\nHappy to discuss! cc @tiangolo @gvbgduh @tomchristie ",
    "closed_at": "2022-09-06T05:43:33Z",
    "created_at": "2019-10-01T20:34:37Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/652",
    "labels": [
      "testclient"
    ],
    "number": 652,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "HTTPX-based TestClient?",
    "user": "florimondmanca"
  },
